/-- **Metric compatibility of the chart Levi-Civita connection on smooth fields.**
For smooth fields `X Y Z`, at every chart point `x`:
`∂ₓ g(Y,Z)(X(x)) = gₓ((∇_X Y)(x), Z(x)) + gₓ(Y(x), (∇_X Z)(x))`,
where the left side is the actual Frechet derivative of the field pairing
`z ↦ g_z(Y(z), Z(z))` along `X(x)`. The proof expands the pairing into its
coefficients, applies the (proved) product rule for Frechet derivatives, and reduces
the Christoffel part to the pointwise algebraic identity `chartMetricCompatible_form`
with the derivative datum instantiated by the derived `dFamily` (which satisfies
`d_symm` by `dFamily_symm`, with no Schwarz hypothesis). -/
theorem nabla_metricCompatible {X Y Z : VectorField ι}
    (hX : ContDiff ℝ ⊤ X) (hY : ContDiff ℝ ⊤ Y) (hZ : ContDiff ℝ ⊤ Z)
    (x : ChartPoint ι) :
    fderiv ℝ (fun z : ChartPoint ι => c.formField z (Y z) (Z z)) x (X x) =
      c.formField x (c.nabla X Y x) (Z x) + c.formField x (Y x) (c.nabla X Z x) := by
```

