dsh: reasoning:
The signature: `Finset.sum_product (s : Finset γ) (t : Finset α) (f : γ × α → β) : (∑ x ∈ s ×ˢ t, f x) = ∑ x ∈ s, ∑ y ∈ t, f (x, y)`. So the f argument is CURRIED-pair: `f : γ × α → β` (not γ → α → β)! That's why `fun j k => f i j k` failed. The direction: `sum_product` : `∑ p in s ×ˢ t, f p = ∑ x in s, ∑ y in t, f (x,y)` — and `sum_product'` : `∑ p in s ×ˢ t, f p.1 p.2 = ∑ x in s, ∑ y in t, f x y` (uncurried).

For my use: I want `∑ i, ∑ j, g i j = ∑ p : ι × ι, g p.1 p.2` — i.e., the reverse of sum_product' with f := g: `sum_product' : ∑ p in univ ×ˢ univ, g p.1 p.2 = ∑ i in univ, ∑ j in univ, g i j`. So `(sum_product' ...).symm : ∑ i, ∑ j, g i j = ∑ p in univ ×ˢ univ, g p.1 p.2` then simp univ×ˢuniv = univ.

So rewrite the lemma proof with sum_product':
```
    (∑ i : ι, ∑ j : ι, ∑ k : ι, f i j k)
        = ∑ q : ι × ι × ι, f q.1 q.2.1 q.2.2 := by
          calc
            (∑ i : ι, ∑ j : ι, ∑ k : ι, f i j k)
                = ∑ i : ι, ∑ p : ι × ι, f i p.1 p.2 := by
                  apply Finset.sum_congr rfl
                  intro i hi
                  simpa using (Finset.sum_product' (s := (Finset.univ : Finset ι))
                    (t := (Finset.univ : Finset ι)) (f := fun j k => f i j k)).symm
            _ = ∑ q : ι × ι × ι, f q.1 q.2.1 q.2.2 := by
                  simpa using (Finset.sum_product' (s := (Finset.univ : Finset ι))
                    (t := (Finset.univ : Finset ι)) (f := fun i p => f i p.1 p.2)).symm
```
And the reverse direction with sum_product' (forward):
```
    (∑ q : ι × ι × ι, f q.1 q.2.1 q.2.2)
        = ∑ k : ι, ∑ i : ι, ∑ j : ι, f k i j := by
          calc
            (∑ q : ι × ι × ι, f q.1 q.2.1 q.2.2)
                = ∑ k : ι, ∑ p : ι × ι, f k p.1 p.2 := by
                  simpa using (Finset.sum_product' (s := (Finset.univ : Finset ι))
                    (t := (Finset.univ : Finset ι)) (f := fun k p => f k p.1 p.2))
            _ = ∑ k : ι, ∑ i : ι, ∑ j : ι, f k i j := by
                  apply Finset.sum_congr rfl
                  intro k hk
                  simpa using (Finset.sum_product' (s := (Finset.univ : Finset ι))
                    (t := (Finset.univ : Finset ι)) (f := fun i j => f k i j))
```
